To commemorate the waning days of summer (here in the northern
hemisphere), is a Stupid Ascension Trick, number 3.4.5: Only wore
beach-wear (Hawaiian shirt and lenses).

However, now that I look at the actual wording from the list of
stupid tricks, I realize that I only did an easy version of it. I
had thought that it implied using only that armor for the ascension,
and so limited myself to not wearing anything other than the shirt
after the Castle. I did wear some other armor while doing the earlier
levels. Sigh. Maybe I'll have to do this one again sometime, to the
more
strict standard.

Anyway, I chose a Tourist, for the starting Hawaiian shirt. I did not
wear any armor other than my starting shirt through all of Gehennom, to

get the Amulet, and all the way up through the Planes and to the final
offering.

